  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Glycolysis turns one glucose into two pyruvate, and it nets two A T P, with or without oxygen."
   ],
   [
    8.112,
    "But look at what it uses along the way."
   ],
   [
    10.208,
    "Two N A D plus take up electrons and become two N A D H."
   ],
   [
    15.43,
    "A cell has only a small supply of N A D plus."
   ],
   [
    18.802,
    "If every one becomes N A D H, and none ever goes back, glycolysis runs out of its helper and stops."
   ],
   [
    26.68,
    "With oxygen, the chain hands those electrons to oxygen, and N A D plus comes back."
   ],
   [
    32.591,
    "Without oxygen, the chain is stuck."
   ],
   [
    34.987,
    "So the cell needs some other way to turn N A D H back into N A D plus."
   ],
   [
    40.586,
    "There are two answers: anaerobic respiration, and fermentation."
   ]
  ]
 },
